WEBVTT

00:00:10.124 --> 00:00:11.952
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.210
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:15.051 --> 00:00:15.687
Mary!

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:16.481
No!

00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:19.452
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.684 --> 00:00:22.075
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:24.145 --> 00:00:25.557
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:27.383
I can't do this alone.

00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:30.788
No!

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:34.510
We got work to do.

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:37.613
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:39.825
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:39.963 --> 00:00:41.910
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:41.993 --> 00:00:43.266
You know, saving people,

00:00:43.349 --> 00:00:44.373
Hunting things,

00:00:44.428 --> 00:00:45.342
Family business.

00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:45.840
No.

00:00:45.951 --> 00:00:47.267
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:47.361 --> 00:00:48.785
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:48.844 --> 00:00:50.228
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:00:50.256 --> 00:00:50.662
Right?

00:00:52.468 --> 00:00:53.668
Yeah. I know.

00:01:35.455 --> 00:01:36.248
Nervous flyer?

00:01:37.104 --> 00:01:38.397
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:39.507 --> 00:01:41.775
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:41.981 --> 00:01:42.749
I mean, what

00:01:42.918 --> 00:01:43.949
20,000 to one?

00:01:47.809 --> 00:01:48.334
Wow.

00:01:49.084 --> 00:01:50.996
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:17.359
Thanks.

00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:18.615
Miranda,

00:02:18.784 --> 00:02:19.421
How are you today?

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:20.842
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:23.616
Welcome aboard.

00:02:24.328 --> 00:02:27.083
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:31.259
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:34.102 --> 00:02:35.470
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:41.442
Um...

00:02:43.241 --> 00:02:44.647
Uh, 11F,

00:02:44.703 --> 00:02:46.615
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:02:48.823 --> 00:02:49.535
...the left.

00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:02.241
Excuse me.

00:03:03.044 --> 00:03:04.319
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:06.793
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:03:07.823 --> 00:03:08.386
Wow.

00:03:08.682 --> 00:03:10.050
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:13.403 --> 00:03:14.115
Excuse me.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.670
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:42.332 --> 00:03:43.661
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:04:55.793 --> 00:04:56.674
Morning, sunshine.

00:04:58.039 --> 00:04:58.807
What time is it?

00:04:58.957 --> 00:05:00.269
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:05:00.419 --> 00:05:01.131
In the morning?

00:05:01.206 --> 00:05:01.600
Yep.

00:05:01.806 --> 00:05:02.871
Where does the day go?

00:05:04.933 --> 00:05:06.020
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:06.226 --> 00:05:07.575
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.288
You, liar

00:05:09.256 --> 00:05:10.381
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:11.131 --> 00:05:12.930
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.808
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:13.864 --> 00:05:14.745
It's riveting tv.

00:05:15.176 --> 00:05:16.563
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:16.807 --> 00:05:17.388
I don't know,

00:05:17.463 --> 00:05:19.053
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:19.241 --> 00:05:19.971
Yeah, it is.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.864
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:21.902 --> 00:05:23.232
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:23.251 --> 00:05:25.781
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:27.198 --> 00:05:28.773
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:34.264 --> 00:05:34.807
Yeah.

00:05:36.585 --> 00:05:38.272
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:38.703 --> 00:05:40.408
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:41.905 --> 00:05:42.805
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:43.123 --> 00:05:45.129
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:46.441 --> 00:05:47.003
So, what?

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:47.603
All this it...

00:05:47.915 --> 00:05:48.946
Never keeps you up at night?

00:05:50.108 --> 00:05:50.576
Never?

00:05:50.932 --> 00:05:51.645
You're never afraid?

00:05:51.926 --> 00:05:52.807
No, not really.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:01.913
That's not fear.

00:06:03.225 --> 00:06:04.125
That is precaution.

00:06:04.706 --> 00:06:05.605
All right, whatever.

00:06:05.643 --> 00:06:06.749
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:15.703 --> 00:06:16.246
Hello?

00:06:16.525 --> 00:06:16.974
Dean,

00:06:17.237 --> 00:06:18.905
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:19.886 --> 00:06:21.901
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:22.985 --> 00:06:23.937
Oh, all right,

00:06:23.981 --> 00:06:26.771
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:27.213 --> 00:06:28.143
It's not back, is it?

00:06:28.342 --> 00:06:28.807
No.

00:06:29.184 --> 00:06:29.715
No.

00:06:30.955 --> 00:06:31.774
Thank god, no.

00:06:33.254 --> 00:06:35.003
But it's something else, and...

00:06:35.512 --> 00:06:36.862
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.058
What is it?

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:39.648
Can we talk in person?

00:06:45.427 --> 00:06:47.176
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:49.823
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:06:50.775 --> 00:06:52.280
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:54.516
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:06:54.583 --> 00:06:55.225
Poltergeist?

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.328
Man, I loved that movie.

00:06:56.372 --> 00:06:58.232
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.907
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:07:02.903 --> 00:07:03.855
Tell you something

00:07:04.493 --> 00:07:05.799
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.061
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:11.033
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:11.652 --> 00:07:12.870
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:13.158 --> 00:07:14.287
Taking some time off.

00:07:14.575 --> 00:07:16.169
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:16.612 --> 00:07:17.962
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:19.331 --> 00:07:19.951
He did?

00:07:20.327 --> 00:07:21.323
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:23.781
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:24.334 --> 00:07:25.309
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.434
He's, um

00:07:28.023 --> 00:07:29.352
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:29.617 --> 00:07:31.145
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:31.411 --> 00:07:32.363
We get sam.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.691
Even trade, huh?

00:07:34.223 --> 00:07:35.684
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:36.304 --> 00:07:37.964
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:39.823 --> 00:07:40.930
I listened to this.

00:07:41.439 --> 00:07:41.926
Well,

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:43.653
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:45.889
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.737
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:07:50.025 --> 00:07:50.933
It was one of ours.

00:07:51.456 --> 00:07:51.905
Mayday

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.221
Took off from here,

00:08:15.783 --> 00:08:17.555
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:19.945
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:20.147 --> 00:08:22.490
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:22.848 --> 00:08:24.145
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:24.931 --> 00:08:26.083
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:27.056 --> 00:08:27.837
Pilot was one.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.380
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:30.962 --> 00:08:31.929
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:33.589 --> 00:08:34.887
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:36.581
Like it was his fault.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:38.223
You don't think it was?

00:08:38.766 --> 00:08:39.614
No, I don't.

00:08:40.334 --> 00:08:40.810
Jerry,

00:08:40.996 --> 00:08:42.836
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:42.921 --> 00:08:44.390
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:44.907
All right.

00:08:45.026 --> 00:08:45.661
And huh...

00:08:45.741 --> 00:08:47.277
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:47.958 --> 00:08:49.190
The other stuff is no problem,

00:08:49.243 --> 00:08:50.064
But the wreckage

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:53.803
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:08:54.782 --> 00:08:56.292
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:08:58.858 --> 00:08:59.348
No problem.

00:09:04.786 --> 00:09:05.237
Hey

00:09:05.395 --> 00:09:05.859
Hi.

00:09:08.825 --> 00:09:09.831
You've been in there forever.

00:09:11.358 --> 00:09:12.391
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:13.132 --> 00:09:14.245
Homeland security?

00:09:15.423 --> 00:09:16.337
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.118
Even for us.

00:09:17.953 --> 00:09:18.456
Yeah, well,

00:09:18.495 --> 00:09:19.820
It's something new, you know?

00:09:19.833 --> 00:09:21.528
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:26.337 --> 00:09:27.260
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:27.479 --> 00:09:28.121
Well,

00:09:28.136 --> 00:09:30.702
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:30.812 --> 00:09:31.156
Yeah?

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:31.735
Listen.

00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:40.429
"No survivors"?

00:09:41.321 --> 00:09:42.051
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:42.061 --> 00:09:43.532
There were seven survivors.

00:09:44.122 --> 00:09:44.748
Got me.

00:09:46.996 --> 00:09:48.514
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:09:48.959 --> 00:09:50.587
There's a long history of spirits and

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:52.638
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:09:52.685 --> 00:09:53.749
Like phantom travelers.

00:09:53.796 --> 00:09:54.203
Mm-Hmm

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.160
Or remember flight 401?

00:09:56.394 --> 00:09:56.848
Right

00:09:57.068 --> 00:09:57.835
The one that crashed,

00:09:57.882 --> 00:09:59.384
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:09:59.447 --> 00:10:00.527
Put it in other planes,

00:10:00.836 --> 00:10:03.074
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:10:03.137 --> 00:10:03.481
Right.

00:10:03.544 --> 00:10:04.029
Yep.

00:10:04.984 --> 00:10:06.205
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:10:06.941 --> 00:10:09.320
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:09.373 --> 00:10:11.094
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:11.188 --> 00:10:11.767
Why him?

00:10:11.814 --> 00:10:13.020
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:13.072 --> 00:10:13.823
And two,

00:10:14.402 --> 00:10:15.780
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:16.421 --> 00:10:16.954
He did.

00:10:18.112 --> 00:10:18.973
What makes you say that?

00:10:19.317 --> 00:10:20.554
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:21.359 --> 00:10:22.706
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:25.447 --> 00:10:26.370
I don't understand.

00:10:26.382 --> 00:10:28.329
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:28.681 --> 00:10:29.270
Right.

00:10:29.776 --> 00:10:31.308
Some new information has come up.

00:10:31.544 --> 00:10:33.464
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:33.669 --> 00:10:35.016
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:35.707 --> 00:10:38.031
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:38.368 --> 00:10:39.092
Like what?

00:10:39.884 --> 00:10:41.113
Strange lights,

00:10:41.787 --> 00:10:43.101
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.208
Voices.

00:10:46.128 --> 00:10:46.936
No, nothing.

00:10:48.869 --> 00:10:49.711
Mr. Joffey

00:10:50.671 --> 00:10:51.143
Jaffey.

00:10:51.446 --> 00:10:51.951
Jaffey.

00:10:52.086 --> 00:10:53.231
You checked yourself in here,

00:10:53.349 --> 00:10:53.804
Right?

00:10:55.019 --> 00:10:55.815
Can I ask why?

00:10:56.312 --> 00:10:57.619
I was a little stressed.

00:10:57.639 --> 00:10:59.490
I survived a plane crash.

00:11:01.156 --> 00:11:01.733
And that's

00:11:01.833 --> 00:11:02.629
What terrified you?

00:11:02.669 --> 00:11:03.803
That's what you were afraid of?

00:11:03.902 --> 00:11:06.410
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:11:06.589 --> 00:11:08.380
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:09.415 --> 00:11:10.410
We need to know what.

00:11:11.478 --> 00:11:11.956
No.

00:11:12.095 --> 00:11:13.170
No, I was...

00:11:13.309 --> 00:11:14.065
Delusional

00:11:14.844 --> 00:11:15.800
Seeing things.

00:11:17.105 --> 00:11:18.125
He was seeing things.

00:11:21.676 --> 00:11:22.271
It's okay.

00:11:23.737 --> 00:11:26.664
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:31.307 --> 00:11:32.038
There was...

00:11:32.277 --> 00:11:32.849
This...

00:11:33.198 --> 00:11:33.866
Man.

00:11:35.551 --> 00:11:36.441
And, uh,

00:11:36.536 --> 00:11:37.951
He had these...

00:11:39.047 --> 00:11:39.670
Eyes...

00:11:39.765 --> 00:11:40.512
These, uh...

00:11:42.587 --> 00:11:43.795
Black eyes.

00:11:45.607 --> 00:11:47.435
And I saw him

00:11:48.215 --> 00:11:50.377
I thought I saw him...

00:11:54.319 --> 00:11:54.923
What?

00:11:57.214 --> 00:11:59.391
He opened the emergency exit.

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:02.190
But that's...

00:12:02.238 --> 00:12:03.351
That's impossible,

00:12:03.764 --> 00:12:05.022
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:12:05.054 --> 00:12:05.944
There's something like

00:12:06.103 --> 00:12:08.200
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:10.364 --> 00:12:10.936
Yeah...

00:12:11.842 --> 00:12:12.732
This man, huh...

00:12:12.812 --> 00:12:15.307
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:15.564 --> 00:12:17.948
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:19.733 --> 00:12:21.052
What are you, nuts?

00:12:23.293 --> 00:12:24.437
He was a passenger.

00:12:24.469 --> 00:12:26.376
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:33.485 --> 00:12:34.645
Say here we are

00:12:34.757 --> 00:12:36.902
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:37.538 --> 00:12:38.047
Hmm.

00:12:39.002 --> 00:12:41.196
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:43.691 --> 00:12:45.725
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:46.109 --> 00:12:49.097
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:12:50.069 --> 00:12:51.086
Not if you're human.

00:12:52.437 --> 00:12:54.423
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:12:54.754 --> 00:12:56.915
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:12:57.344 --> 00:12:59.124
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:13:07.756 --> 00:13:09.059
This is your late husband?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.523
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:12.344 --> 00:13:13.441
And you said he was a...

00:13:14.299 --> 00:13:15.094
Dentist?

00:13:15.514 --> 00:13:16.097
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:17.374 --> 00:13:19.683
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:22.547 --> 00:13:24.594
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:28.257 --> 00:13:29.666
For him to go like that...

00:13:32.313 --> 00:13:33.553
How long were you married?

00:13:35.957 --> 00:13:37.159
13 years.

00:13:37.916 --> 00:13:39.118
In all that time,

00:13:40.714 --> 00:13:42.442
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:42.836 --> 00:13:44.339
Strange about him,

00:13:44.864 --> 00:13:46.479
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:13:49.684 --> 00:13:50.379
Well...

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:54.682
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:13:54.813 --> 00:13:55.883
If that's what you mean.

00:14:00.017 --> 00:14:01.202
I mean it goes without saying.

00:14:01.221 --> 00:14:02.635
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:14:03.037 --> 00:14:04.652
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:14:04.671 --> 00:14:06.399
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:14:07.169 --> 00:14:09.310
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:09.328 --> 00:14:10.812
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:12.654 --> 00:14:13.555
Okay.

00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:14.764
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:14.793 --> 00:14:15.638
We'd better look the part.

00:14:22.016 --> 00:14:24.253
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:24.572 --> 00:14:25.398
No, you don't.

00:14:25.886 --> 00:14:27.107
You look more like a...

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.854
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:31.694 --> 00:14:32.896
I hate this thing.

00:14:32.933 --> 00:14:33.365
Hey.

00:14:33.741 --> 00:14:35.450
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:19.444 --> 00:15:20.158
What is that?

00:15:21.322 --> 00:15:22.487
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:22.937 --> 00:15:24.646
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:25.437 --> 00:15:27.291
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:27.309 --> 00:15:29.751
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:30.804 --> 00:15:32.006
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:32.757 --> 00:15:33.714
It's homemade.

00:15:35.818 --> 00:15:37.677
Yeah, I can see that.

00:16:04.219 --> 00:16:05.778
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:11.433 --> 00:16:12.372
What is this stuff?

00:16:12.503 --> 00:16:13.818
One way to find out.

00:16:26.681 --> 00:16:27.864
Homeland security?

00:16:28.697 --> 00:16:29.166
What?

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:30.706
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:31.345 --> 00:16:32.190
What are you talking about?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.539
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:14.927 --> 00:17:16.918
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:18.439 --> 00:17:19.209
Listen Chuck

00:17:19.378 --> 00:17:20.429
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:20.977 --> 00:17:22.460
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:22.779 --> 00:17:23.606
Not even a horse

00:17:23.756 --> 00:17:24.545
More like a pony.

00:17:25.561 --> 00:17:26.481
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.490
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:29.411 --> 00:17:30.218
Look, Chuck,

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:31.927
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:32.303 --> 00:17:33.110
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:34.032 --> 00:17:34.746
No, the...

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:36.849
The waiting is worse.

00:17:39.328 --> 00:17:41.169
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:14.365 --> 00:18:14.928
Huh.

00:18:16.599 --> 00:18:18.045
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:18.327 --> 00:18:18.947
You're sure?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.487
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:20.506 --> 00:18:21.876
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:21.876 --> 00:18:23.210
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:23.247 --> 00:18:24.675
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:31.603 --> 00:18:31.998
Hmm.

00:18:32.974 --> 00:18:35.754
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:35.857 --> 00:18:36.833
Demonic possession?

00:18:37.378 --> 00:18:40.495
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:40.666 --> 00:18:42.074
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:42.318 --> 00:18:43.013
It's possible.

00:18:43.316 --> 00:18:45.701
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:46.602
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:46.659 --> 00:18:48.180
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:18:48.217 --> 00:18:50.152
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:18:50.283 --> 00:18:51.992
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:18:52.182 --> 00:18:52.707
Never.

00:18:58.623 --> 00:18:59.299
I'm ready.

00:18:59.506 --> 00:19:00.332
Let's do this.

00:19:08.588 --> 00:19:09.395
How you feeling?

00:19:09.658 --> 00:19:10.466
I feel great.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.531
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:12.907 --> 00:19:13.752
I hope so.

00:19:17.472 --> 00:19:18.298
How long we been up?

00:19:18.862 --> 00:19:20.608
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:20.965 --> 00:19:21.416
Wow.

00:19:21.773 --> 00:19:22.768
Time really does fly.

00:19:50.049 --> 00:19:50.669
So,

00:19:51.063 --> 00:19:53.166
Every religion in every world culture

00:19:53.223 --> 00:19:56.077
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:19:56.426 --> 00:19:59.374
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:19:59.468 --> 00:20:01.140
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:20:01.234 --> 00:20:02.360
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:20:02.398 --> 00:20:03.806
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:20:03.844 --> 00:20:06.567
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:20:06.612 --> 00:20:07.476
Both natural

00:20:07.589 --> 00:20:08.453
And man-Made

00:20:08.509 --> 00:20:10.762
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:10.781 --> 00:20:12.340
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:16.607 --> 00:20:17.771
All right, so, what?

00:20:17.809 --> 00:20:19.837
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:19.875 --> 00:20:21.602
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:22.522 --> 00:20:23.106
Yeah.

00:20:24.252 --> 00:20:24.853
You know,

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:28.120
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:33.026 --> 00:20:33.533
What?

00:20:35.091 --> 00:20:37.082
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:37.645 --> 00:20:39.298
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:39.373 --> 00:20:41.251
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:42.246 --> 00:20:42.960
This is big.

00:20:44.389 --> 00:20:45.516
I wish dad was here.

00:20:46.587 --> 00:20:47.845
Yeah. Me too.

00:20:54.609 --> 00:20:54.984
Hello?

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.167
Dean it's Jerry

00:20:56.355 --> 00:20:57.069
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:20:57.369 --> 00:20:58.327
My pilot friend...

00:21:00.318 --> 00:21:01.444
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:21:03.437 --> 00:21:03.925
Wha...

00:21:04.301 --> 00:21:05.446
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.850
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:21:07.925 --> 00:21:08.939
About an hour ago.

00:21:09.578 --> 00:21:10.423
The plane went down.

00:21:10.799 --> 00:21:11.587
Where'd this happen?

00:21:11.907 --> 00:21:14.066
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:14.632 --> 00:21:16.078
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:16.322 --> 00:21:16.885
I'm sorry?

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:17.637
Nothing.

00:21:18.369 --> 00:21:20.303
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.258
Another crash?

00:21:23.465 --> 00:21:23.990
Yeah.

00:21:24.366 --> 00:21:24.836
Let's go.

00:21:25.042 --> 00:21:25.587
Where?

00:21:26.282 --> 00:21:26.901
Nazareth.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:39.792
Sulfur?

00:21:42.498 --> 00:21:43.681
Well, that's great.

00:21:44.414 --> 00:21:47.174
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:49.278
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:21:49.684 --> 00:21:50.773
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:21:51.863 --> 00:21:53.966
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:21:54.379 --> 00:21:55.186
What's the bad news?

00:21:55.374 --> 00:21:57.947
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:21:58.112 --> 00:21:58.995
And get this

00:21:59.145 --> 00:22:00.741
So did flight 2485.

00:22:01.042 --> 00:22:01.849
40 minutes?

00:22:02.262 --> 00:22:02.938
What does that mean?

00:22:03.521 --> 00:22:04.835
It's biblical numerology.

00:22:05.098 --> 00:22:07.089
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:22:07.145 --> 00:22:08.122
The number means death.

00:22:08.518 --> 00:22:09.250
I went back,

00:22:09.325 --> 00:22:11.992
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:14.809
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:15.861 --> 00:22:16.743
Any survivors?

00:22:17.419 --> 00:22:17.889
No.

00:22:18.331 --> 00:22:18.856
Or not

00:22:18.932 --> 00:22:20.002
Until now,at least

00:22:20.021 --> 00:22:22.312
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:23.363 --> 00:22:24.809
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:24.922 --> 00:22:26.180
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:26.481 --> 00:22:27.345
"No survivors."

00:22:31.331 --> 00:22:32.702
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:33.922 --> 00:22:35.012
Something finish the job.

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:39.427
Really?

00:22:40.046 --> 00:22:41.812
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:43.145
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:43.164 --> 00:22:46.018
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:46.751 --> 00:22:47.220
Thanks.

00:22:47.671 --> 00:22:48.309
All right.

00:22:48.424 --> 00:22:51.072
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:22:51.186 --> 00:22:52.557
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:22:52.614 --> 00:22:55.149
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:22:55.412 --> 00:22:55.937
Right

00:22:55.975 --> 00:22:58.078
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:22:58.116 --> 00:22:59.675
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:22:59.712 --> 00:23:01.064
That sounds like just our luck.

00:23:01.383 --> 00:23:02.998
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:23:03.129 --> 00:23:04.575
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:23:05.159 --> 00:23:06.724
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:23:06.742 --> 00:23:08.066
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:08.121 --> 00:23:09.482
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.587
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:14.382
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:14.438 --> 00:23:15.127
We'll make it.

00:23:29.462 --> 00:23:30.096
Right there.

00:23:30.208 --> 00:23:31.326
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:31.475 --> 00:23:32.052
Okay.

00:23:32.593 --> 00:23:33.953
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:34.004 --> 00:23:34.992
We need to find a phone.

00:23:38.175 --> 00:23:39.107
Airport Services.

00:23:39.218 --> 00:23:40.299
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:40.369 --> 00:23:41.524
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:41.636 --> 00:23:43.253
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:43.275 --> 00:23:45.168
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:45.311 --> 00:23:46.588
Flight 424.

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:47.755
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:23:48.019 --> 00:23:49.737
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:23:49.825 --> 00:23:51.630
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:23:54.569 --> 00:23:55.626
Come on.

00:23:57.233 --> 00:23:58.467
This is amanda walker.

00:23:58.841 --> 00:23:59.611
Miss walker.

00:24:00.052 --> 00:24:01.862
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:24:01.884 --> 00:24:04.064
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:24:04.394 --> 00:24:06.222
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:07.125
Why Karen?

00:24:07.169 --> 00:24:09.282
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:09.317 --> 00:24:10.836
But she was injured, so

00:24:10.968 --> 00:24:13.962
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:17.227 --> 00:24:17.844
You what?

00:24:17.932 --> 00:24:18.790
Five minutes ago.

00:24:18.834 --> 00:24:21.499
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:21.521 --> 00:24:22.467
Who is this?

00:24:23.668 --> 00:24:24.681
Uh, well...

00:24:25.099 --> 00:24:26.200
There must be some mistake.

00:24:26.222 --> 00:24:28.248
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:29.987 --> 00:24:31.594
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:33.243 --> 00:24:34.322
Guilty as charged.

00:24:35.136 --> 00:24:37.206
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:38.065 --> 00:24:39.694
He's really sorry.

00:24:40.333 --> 00:24:41.918
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:41.962 --> 00:24:43.723
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:43.811 --> 00:24:44.733
Yes, but...

00:24:45.085 --> 00:24:46.758
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:47.089 --> 00:24:47.815
So

00:24:47.925 --> 00:24:49.401
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:24:49.599 --> 00:24:50.634
Don't be like that.

00:24:51.098 --> 00:24:52.199
Come on. The guy's

00:24:52.354 --> 00:24:53.983
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:24:55.326 --> 00:24:56.009
Really?

00:24:56.229 --> 00:24:56.977
Oh, yeah.

00:24:57.638 --> 00:24:59.157
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:24:59.168 --> 00:25:01.260
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:25:01.414 --> 00:25:03.176
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:09.892 --> 00:25:10.817
How are you?

00:25:12.226 --> 00:25:13.393
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:21.370 --> 00:25:22.272
Damn it!

00:25:22.779 --> 00:25:23.858
So close.

00:25:26.368 --> 00:25:28.063
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:28.537 --> 00:25:29.594
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:29.704 --> 00:25:31.377
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:31.476 --> 00:25:32.092
Dean,

00:25:32.225 --> 00:25:33.392
That plane is leaving

00:25:33.436 --> 00:25:34.955
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:34.977 --> 00:25:35.902
And if we're right,

00:25:36.541 --> 00:25:37.840
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:37.994 --> 00:25:38.632
I know.

00:25:38.743 --> 00:25:39.315
Okay.

00:25:39.408 --> 00:25:42.094
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:42.138 --> 00:25:44.274
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:44.318 --> 00:25:45.507
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:45.573 --> 00:25:46.872
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:25:48.876 --> 00:25:49.889
Are you okay?

00:25:52.256 --> 00:25:53.533
No, not really.

00:25:54.810 --> 00:25:55.955
What? What's wrong?

00:25:58.124 --> 00:26:00.150
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:26:02.285 --> 00:26:03.100
Flying?

00:26:03.519 --> 00:26:05.236
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:26:05.578 --> 00:26:06.436
You're joking, right?

00:26:06.502 --> 00:26:07.647
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:09.431 --> 00:26:11.016
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:12.139 --> 00:26:13.923
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:14.212 --> 00:26:14.608
What?

00:26:14.630 --> 00:26:15.665
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:16.216 --> 00:26:17.008
Are you, nuts?

00:26:17.559 --> 00:26:18.924
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:18.968 --> 00:26:20.972
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:21.016 --> 00:26:22.887
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:23.658 --> 00:26:24.583
Come on!

00:26:26.279 --> 00:26:26.962
Really?

00:26:29.274 --> 00:26:30.132
Man...

00:26:43.056 --> 00:26:45.015
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:14.878 --> 00:27:15.847
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:15.869 --> 00:27:17.014
Calms me down.

00:27:19.172 --> 00:27:20.031
Look, man,

00:27:20.405 --> 00:27:21.528
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:21.550 --> 00:27:23.113
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:24.452 --> 00:27:24.959
Okay.

00:27:24.981 --> 00:27:25.883
I mean, we got

00:27:25.994 --> 00:27:28.834
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:28.878 --> 00:27:32.159
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:32.181 --> 00:27:34.360
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:34.449 --> 00:27:36.078
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:37.792 --> 00:27:38.540
Now,

00:27:38.662 --> 00:27:40.687
Who is it possessing?

00:27:41.766 --> 00:27:43.020
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:43.021 --> 00:27:44.078
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:46.214
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:46.621 --> 00:27:49.395
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:27:51.476 --> 00:27:52.071
Well,

00:27:52.269 --> 00:27:54.030
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:27:54.074 --> 00:27:55.682
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:27:55.748 --> 00:27:56.452
Mm-Hmm.

00:27:58.324 --> 00:27:59.204
Excuse me.

00:27:59.730 --> 00:28:00.479
Are you Amanda?

00:28:00.633 --> 00:28:01.470
No, I'm not.

00:28:01.514 --> 00:28:03.341
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:09.265 --> 00:28:11.313
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:12.106 --> 00:28:13.162
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:13.295 --> 00:28:15.342
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:15.783 --> 00:28:17.082
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:18.427 --> 00:28:19.880
There's ways to test that.

00:28:22.082 --> 00:28:23.337
I brought holy water.

00:28:24.218 --> 00:28:25.957
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:26.424 --> 00:28:28.604
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:29.176 --> 00:28:30.123
Oh. Nice.

00:28:32.259 --> 00:28:32.941
Hey.

00:28:33.107 --> 00:28:33.789
What?

00:28:33.965 --> 00:28:34.846
Say it in latin.

00:28:35.132 --> 00:28:35.793
I know.

00:28:35.881 --> 00:28:36.453
Okay.

00:28:36.696 --> 00:28:37.334
Hey!

00:28:37.841 --> 00:28:38.655
What?!

00:28:38.964 --> 00:28:40.791
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:40.901 --> 00:28:42.707
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:28:55.582 --> 00:28:56.705
Hi. Hi.

00:28:57.762 --> 00:28:58.841
Can I help you with something?

00:28:58.929 --> 00:28:59.832
Oh, no.

00:28:59.876 --> 00:29:01.835
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:03.851
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:29:03.961 --> 00:29:05.899
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:29:06.647 --> 00:29:09.686
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:10.820 --> 00:29:12.009
You'd be surprised.

00:29:12.339 --> 00:29:14.276
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:14.959 --> 00:29:16.610
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:17.953 --> 00:29:19.605
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:19.946 --> 00:29:21.025
You're scared to fly?

00:29:22.147 --> 00:29:23.381
Kind of a long story.

00:29:24.514 --> 00:29:26.100
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:26.177 --> 00:29:26.981
It's okay.

00:29:28.335 --> 00:29:29.942
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:31.219 --> 00:29:32.034
No.

00:29:32.562 --> 00:29:34.214
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:34.269 --> 00:29:35.656
I just, uh...

00:29:36.449 --> 00:29:38.408
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:39.685 --> 00:29:40.412
Huh.

00:29:41.436 --> 00:29:42.074
So...

00:29:44.893 --> 00:29:45.685
Cristo.

00:29:46.984 --> 00:29:48.305
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:29:53.547 --> 00:29:54.405
Cristo?

00:29:55.572 --> 00:29:56.783
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:29:57.818 --> 00:29:59.095
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:30:03.296 --> 00:30:04.155
Okay.

00:30:12.100 --> 00:30:14.962
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:15.006 --> 00:30:16.063
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:16.107 --> 00:30:17.439
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:17.461 --> 00:30:19.024
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:19.090 --> 00:30:20.874
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:21.006 --> 00:30:22.063
Anywhere.

00:30:22.856 --> 00:30:25.035
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:25.113 --> 00:30:27.447
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:27.777 --> 00:30:29.340
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:29.385 --> 00:30:30.838
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:30.926 --> 00:30:32.709
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:32.753 --> 00:30:34.063
Yes, you can.

00:30:34.459 --> 00:30:37.388
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:37.432 --> 00:30:38.489
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:38.533 --> 00:30:39.744
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:39.766 --> 00:30:41.836
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:41.946 --> 00:30:42.936
Right now.

00:30:51.901 --> 00:30:52.694
Good.

00:30:53.971 --> 00:30:54.719
Now,

00:30:55.325 --> 00:30:57.659
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:30:58.254 --> 00:30:59.487
The ritual romano.

00:31:00.544 --> 00:31:01.424
What do we have to do?

00:31:01.887 --> 00:31:02.680
It's two parts.

00:31:02.724 --> 00:31:05.146
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:31:05.301 --> 00:31:08.405
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:09.451
More powerful?

00:31:09.561 --> 00:31:10.463
Yeah. How?

00:31:11.146 --> 00:31:12.599
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:12.643 --> 00:31:14.471
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:14.735 --> 00:31:16.298
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:16.827 --> 00:31:18.808
Well, because the second part

00:31:19.689 --> 00:31:21.164
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:21.561 --> 00:31:22.728
Once and for all.

00:31:24.247 --> 00:31:25.942
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:32:03.491 --> 00:32:04.423
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:32:04.531 --> 00:32:05.333
Anything?

00:32:05.527 --> 00:32:07.390
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:32:07.650 --> 00:32:08.538
15 minutes.

00:32:09.795 --> 00:32:11.116
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:11.874 --> 00:32:13.390
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:14.660 --> 00:32:15.613
You believe that?

00:32:16.371 --> 00:32:17.454
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:26.958 --> 00:32:27.933
What? What is it?

00:32:29.255 --> 00:32:29.969
Cristo.

00:32:45.116 --> 00:32:46.286
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:46.437 --> 00:32:47.476
12 minutes, dude.

00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:50.735
Oh, hi.

00:32:51.491 --> 00:32:53.084
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:32:53.157 --> 00:32:55.330
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:32:55.547 --> 00:32:57.430
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:32:57.913 --> 00:32:59.507
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:32:59.871 --> 00:33:02.165
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:33:02.213 --> 00:33:04.362
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:33:06.098 --> 00:33:07.040
Who are you guys?

00:33:07.160 --> 00:33:09.309
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:09.430 --> 00:33:11.820
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:11.893 --> 00:33:12.907
We need your help

00:33:12.979 --> 00:33:14.694
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:14.814 --> 00:33:15.716
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:15.788 --> 00:33:18.638
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:20.110
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:20.255 --> 00:33:21.631
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:21.752 --> 00:33:24.039
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:24.160 --> 00:33:25.029
He's dead.

00:33:25.712 --> 00:33:26.750
Wait. What?

00:33:26.919 --> 00:33:28.126
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:28.416 --> 00:33:29.961
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:30.106 --> 00:33:31.652
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:31.676 --> 00:33:33.318
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:34.066 --> 00:33:35.853
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:35.878 --> 00:33:37.203
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:37.228 --> 00:33:38.628
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:38.653 --> 00:33:40.303
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:45.609 --> 00:33:46.534
On...

00:33:47.484 --> 00:33:49.209
On 2485,

00:33:49.259 --> 00:33:51.059
There was this man.

00:33:51.109 --> 00:33:53.234
He...had these eyes.

00:33:53.509 --> 00:33:55.162
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:33:55.184 --> 00:33:56.837
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:33:56.859 --> 00:33:58.648
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:33:58.693 --> 00:34:00.754
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:34:00.821 --> 00:34:01.750
Don't have time to explain.

00:34:01.772 --> 00:34:03.199
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:34:03.312 --> 00:34:04.693
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:34:04.738 --> 00:34:06.572
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:34:06.617 --> 00:34:08.293
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:08.338 --> 00:34:09.719
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:09.787 --> 00:34:11.213
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:11.236 --> 00:34:13.410
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:20.008 --> 00:34:20.755
Okay.

00:35:00.834 --> 00:35:01.989
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:08.170 --> 00:35:10.841
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:10.887 --> 00:35:12.358
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:21.397 --> 00:35:22.718
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:22.784 --> 00:35:23.709
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:23.753 --> 00:35:25.537
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:25.581 --> 00:35:27.166
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:27.210 --> 00:35:28.487
Can you do that?

00:35:28.795 --> 00:35:29.380
Amanda?

00:35:29.623 --> 00:35:30.177
Okay.

00:35:30.907 --> 00:35:31.483
Okay.

00:35:33.161 --> 00:35:35.331
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:35:57.248 --> 00:35:58.842
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:36:00.768 --> 00:36:02.318
She must have died screaming!

00:36:03.004 --> 00:36:04.642
Even now, she's burning!

00:36:07.551 --> 00:36:08.260
Sam!

00:36:11.865 --> 00:36:13.038
"Prayer"...

00:36:15.761 --> 00:36:16.470
I got him.

00:36:37.398 --> 00:36:38.018
Where'd he go?

00:36:38.085 --> 00:36:38.992
He's in the plane.

00:36:39.059 --> 00:36:40.564
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:27.895 --> 00:38:28.426
I don't know.

00:38:28.515 --> 00:38:29.733
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:29.976 --> 00:38:31.283
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:31.570 --> 00:38:33.740
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:35.751 --> 00:38:36.902
Anything else?

00:38:37.279 --> 00:38:38.186
No, that's all.

00:38:41.968 --> 00:38:42.920
"Thank you"

00:38:49.318 --> 00:38:50.337
Let's get out of here.

00:38:53.281 --> 00:38:54.123
You okay?

00:38:55.827 --> 00:38:56.580
Dean,

00:38:58.550 --> 00:39:00.166
It knew about Jessica.

00:39:02.841 --> 00:39:05.210
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:39:05.586 --> 00:39:06.317
They lie.

00:39:07.091 --> 00:39:08.309
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:09.992 --> 00:39:10.612
Yeah.

00:39:13.054 --> 00:39:13.829
Come on.

00:39:20.028 --> 00:39:22.370
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:23.787 --> 00:39:25.470
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:26.931 --> 00:39:28.277
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:28.808 --> 00:39:30.137
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:33.369 --> 00:39:34.344
You know, Jerry.

00:39:34.676 --> 00:39:35.251
Yeah.

00:39:35.867 --> 00:39:38.480
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:38.524 --> 00:39:40.162
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:40.428 --> 00:39:41.624
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:42.266 --> 00:39:42.704
What?

00:39:42.749 --> 00:39:44.077
When did you talk to him?

00:39:44.254 --> 00:39:46.690
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:47.110 --> 00:39:49.767
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:39:51.711 --> 00:39:52.508
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:09.400 --> 00:40:10.884
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:10.906 --> 00:40:13.054
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:13.077 --> 00:40:14.383
It's been out of service.

00:40:15.706 --> 00:40:16.902
This is John Winchester.

00:40:17.234 --> 00:40:18.540
I can't be reached.

00:40:18.549 --> 00:40:20.896
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:21.848 --> 00:40:26.648

866-907-3235

00:40:27.644 --> 00:40:28.729
He'll can help.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
